# The framework's own test entry, written as data for the framework's generic
# entry (gezi.contest.entry.generic.GenericEntryProvider). The judge's
# tests (contest-judge) and the benchmarks of jmh-pipeline
# (CompiledRunBenchmark) read it, so that a framework test does not break
# when a player changes an entry. It is never a competitor: no contest round
# reads it. It replaces the deleted baseline entry
# (https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1642), whose knowledge and
# three rounds it keeps.
#
# Its knowledge is the native route's that the strategies' and the JIT's
# tests saturate with (the rounds of tests/round_fixtures), small and stable:
# the Prolog backend's preset, its backend and the native typing of the types
# it represents, with the knowledge files of the two other rounds. The rounds,
# in order: closure_application, the type check of the Prolog backend's
# preset (its member prolog_backend_type_check), and occurrence_erasure. The
# files are imported from corpora/compiler, as tests/round_fixtures imports
# them, and not through tests/round_fixtures: the judge's sandbox binds
# corpora and the entry's directory only, so an entry run by the judge reads
# nothing under tests.
#
# Each round enables every built-in rule (`rules`), closes no closure
# (`opening` false), and its leaves are those of every knowledge file of the
# entry (a contribution to the slot leaves that reads every file's leaves). The JIT's options are solo's: fallback dispatch,
# the closure backend, the instance table with trial 1024 and a young
# generation of 2^19, and the rest of solo's options; each round's
# implementations are solo's too. The executor that reads the programs is
# the framework's JIT (the executor jit of
# corpora/compiler/entry_options/executor).
#
# The file is read by projection off the tree whose visible subtree is
# Gezi's directory (StandardLibrary.entryTerm), in the scope of
# gezi.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" off the variable gezi, the name https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1924
# of the project root's own directory; they break if that directory is renamed.
